<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husain Shah Langah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Husain Langah I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Husain Shah</a> Langah was the most important ruler of the Langah Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> in the second half of the 15th century. During a reign of about three decades he repelled attacks by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahlul-lodi">Bahlul Lodi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and extended his rule along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, while Multan flourished as a centre of trade and learning.</p></div>
